<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="recommended-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_defend.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Recommended Gear for Protection Warriors in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="what-is-the-bis-protection-warrior-gear">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_warrior_revenge.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> What is the BiS Protection Warrior gear?</h3>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>The <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warrior</span> stat priority may seem simple in theory. Still, it is ever complicated by the different roles a <span class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_warrior.gif");'></span>
<span class="c1">Protection Warrior</span> can fulfill, and by the era of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=84840/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a>, the emphasis on damage output by tanks is increasing. Our quest for the <b>"best gear"</b> is not only complicated by trying to balance survivability and offensive utility. Additionally, even if you were to prioritize full defense, your stat priority will change based on how you choose to utilize your active mitigation. <br/>
<br/>Everything from talents to gear to enchants belongs on a spectrum between full beef-mode and full DPS-mode, and where each individual falls on that spectrum will be different depending on how comfortable you are with the class, what type of content you're aiming to do, along with how much trust you have in the rest of your raid. <b>
<i>It's unlikely that being towards either side of that spectrum will be the best thing for you and your raid group</i></b>, so make gearing adjustments that fit within the context of how you approach the game. <br/>
<br/>I recommend familiarizing yourself with the <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/classes/warrior/protection/tank-stat-priority-pve">Protection Warrior Stat Priority</a> before considering your best-in-slot loot. Generally, we'll prefer gear that favors <b>Parry</b> and <b>Dodge</b>, but different encounters will call for different gear. While raid drops are generally the most reliable way of getting high item level gear, many other items can be just as good, if not better.<ul class="exclude-units"></ul>
<br/>
<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="bis-gear">Overall Best in Slot Gear for Protection Warriors</h3>A tank will have many different approaches when it comes to gearing, and the following gearsets will cater to a balanced and offensive approach. However, that doesn't mean that you should limit yourself to gear only for a specific set of gear. At times, you may require a slightly more defensive set, and other times you can afford to lean more heavily into offensive throughput. <br/>
<br/>We've opted not to include a full defensive set in the list below, as it's almost identical to the balanced set. Using a second trinket with slightly more defensive utility, along with stamina shoulder and leg enchants, will get you the most defensive possible outcome while still providing decent offensive utility.<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
