<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="set-bonuses">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_treasurechest02b.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Tier &amp; Set Bonuses for Protection Warriors in Mists of Pandaria Classic</span></h2>The lack of self-sustain has always been a downside of the Protection Warrior, and the tier 16 2-set does a decent amount of work to combat that issue. You heal for 30% of all damage blocked with a shield and 30% of all damage absorbed by <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=112048/shield-barrier">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_shield_07.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Barrier</span></a>.<br/>
<br/>In high <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=132365/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> environments, this set bonus can provide very high healing, especially in a 10-man environment where the healing cadence on the tank is significantly slower than 25-man. In an extremely high Vengeance environment, however, the absorb from Shield Barrier very rarely breaks. This is, of course, a good "issue" to have, but it does mean that the value from the 2-set is reduced in these situations. <br/>
<br/>The 4-set bonus, which increases our rage generation after <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1160/demoralizing-shout">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_warcry.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demoralizing Shout</span></a> fades from the target, is mediocre at best, and is not good enough to justify over the 6 additional item levels of other alternatives. <br/>
<br/>Additionally, every single tier piece except the legs has mastery as one of its stats, which is a very poor stat for Protection Warriors outside of niche situations.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="tier-16-tank">
