<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>As with the <span class="q5">legendary meta gem</span>, we have access to both an offensive and defensive option when it comes to the legendary cloaks. <br/>
<br/>
<b>Which should you use? </b>Well, the answer is not black and white. As you head into Siege of Orgimmar progression, most people should default to <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>, especially for the later bosses. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a> operates as a cheat death with a 2-minute cooldown. It's unique in the way that it functions, however. If you have 90% health, take a massive swing that would've killed you; the cloak will absorb the entire hit, leaving you at 90% health after the cloak procs. On the flip side, if you are tanking many small adds and have 2% health before taking a fatal hit, the cloak will put you back at 2% health, which will likely not save you from dying. If you do happen to die while the effect of the cloak is on cooldown, the cooldown will be cleared when you resurrect.  <br/>
<br/>This cloak should be used when you're expecting to take large hits in fights such as Garrosh Hellscream, Paragons of the Klaxxi, and Iron Juggernaut. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> procs a continuous frontal cleave approximately two times per minute. This effect scales with Attack Power from <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a> and is responsible for approximately 5% of your overall damage on single target encounters. Where this effect shines is on encounters where cleave damage is valued or where you are very unlikely to make use of the cheat death effect of <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102250/qian-ying-fortitude-of-niuzao">
<img alt="Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_oxtank_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Qian-Ying, Fortitude of Niuzao</span></a>. <br/>
<br/>This cloak should be used when offensive throughput is valued on multiple targets on fights like <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=71889/secured-stockpile-of-pandaren-spoils">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Secured Stockpile of Pandaren Spoils</span></a> and <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=72249/galakras">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Galakras</span></a>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Protection Warrior Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>Trinkets become very interesting in SoO, as there are a lot of niche interactions that can completely change rotations and the way you approach a fight. That being said, the philosophy around trinkets and gearing hasn't changed. Trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105568/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> will give you the most survivability, while trinkets like <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> will give you the most offensive utility. What trinket one should use will depend on the encounter and overall tanking philosophy. <br/>
<br/>Unlike other plate tanks, however, the Protection Warrior gets disproportionate value from crit, both offensively and defensively, making the best offensive alternatives very attractive defensively as well. <br/>
<br/>Changing trinkets on an encounter-by-encounter basis is encouraged.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>
<ins>Offensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a> - This is an all-around great trinket that almost puts us at near 100% crit rate towards the tail-end of the effect. In a more balanced build, this is by far your best trinket, but it loses a bit of value in a crit-oriented offensive build.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105609/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> - This is generally our second strongest offensive trinket, but in a fully offensive gear set up, it will outperform <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105632/skeers-bloodsoaked-talisman">
<img alt="Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Skeer's Bloodsoaked Talisman</span></a>. We value this trinket almost entirely because of the critical strike damage modifier, as haste and mastery are very poor stats for us as Protection Warriors.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105527/haromms-talisman">
<img alt="Haromm's Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_08.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Haromm's Talisman</span></a> - Yes, we're back to including agility trinkets on our BIS lists. This trinket is great simply due to the Multistrike effect. Agility does give a very small amount of crit to a strength-based user, but this trinket should be prioritized to other agility users. It's worth mentioning that in a balanced build, this trinket is prefered to <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105609/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105645/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a> - Despite being a stamina trinket, it has quite strong offensive utility for a Protection Warrior due to how well we scale with crit. This trinket is for those who lean slightly more defensively in their gearing.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105459/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> - This trinket is simply a niche trinket that excels in fights where there are a lot of targets for you to cleave. Bosses like Spoils and Galakras stand out as great fights for this trinket.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96915/gaze-of-the-twins">
<img alt="Gaze of the Twins" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_spectralsight.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gaze of the Twins</span></a> - This is your strongest offensive trinket from the previous phase. Because of how low the item level is compared to the newer alternatives, it is not competitive with any of the other trinkets on this list, except that it has slightly higher throughput than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105645/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a>.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Defensive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105568/vial-of-living-corruption">
<img alt="Vial of Living Corruption" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_10.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vial of Living Corruption</span></a> - This is your strongest defensive trinket, reducing the cooldown of the following abilities by up to 25%: <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=871/shield-wall">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_shieldwall.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Shield Wall</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1719/recklessness">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_criticalstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Recklessness</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=1160/demoralizing-shout">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_warcry.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Demoralizing Shout</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=12975/last-stand">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_ashestoashes.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Last Stand</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=52174/heroic-leap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_heroicleap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heroic Leap</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=114192/mocking-banner">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/mocking_banner.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Mocking Banner</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105438/rooks-unlucky-talisman">
<img alt="Rook's Unlucky Talisman" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Rook's Unlucky Talisman</span></a> - This trinket has incredible situational use due to its long duration and short cooldown. Of course, only a few things that are considered AOE are dangerous for tanks, but one clear example of where it shines is if you're looking to soak <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=144969/annihilate">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/sha_spell_fire_bluehellfire.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Annihilate</span></a> during the <a data-entity="npc" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/npc=71865/garrosh-hellscream">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Garrosh Hellscream</span></a> intermissions for additional <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=93099/vengeance">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_shadow_charm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vengeance</span></a>.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105645/curse-of-hubris">
<img alt="Curse of Hubris" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_04.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Curse of Hubris</span></a> - This trinket makes it on both the lists due to its strong defensive utility through stamina, and strong offensive utility through the crit on-use.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105514/juggernauts-focusing-crystal">
<img alt="Juggernaut's Focusing Crystal" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_19.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Juggernaut's Focusing Crystal</span></a> - This trinket turns all of your offensive abilities into a small heal on yourself. In practice, the healing is quite negligible, and offers limited utility outside of a few circumstances.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=96927/soul-barrier">
<img alt="Soul Barrier" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_warlock_demonsoul.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Soul Barrier</span></a> - The on-use effect of this trinket is incredibly undertuned and does nothing essentially; however, the stamina alone on the trinket makes it a strong contender defensively, especially during progression.</div></li></ul>
<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="emperor-shaohao">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/achievement_faction_shadopan_assault.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Emperor Shaohao</span></h3>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>
<div class="pad exclude-units"></div>Emperor Shaohao is a new faction introduced on the Timeless Isle.  This faction is purely for vanity loot only.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Protection Warrior</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria, your Hit cap is 7.5% Hit and 15% Expertise. Keep in mind that some abilities, such as the <span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" data-contiguous="true" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/race_draenei_female.gif");'></span> Draenei Racial Heroic Presence, will contribute to your overall Hit and/<wbr/>or Expertise needed.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="hit-rating">Hit Rating</h4>At 7.5% Hit, your attacks will no longer be able to miss Raid bosses. We prioritize Hit in our gearing, as even though it scales linearly to Expertise, some abilities, like <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=6343/thunder-clap">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_nature_thunderclap.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thunder Clap</span></a>, can miss but can't be dodged or parried.<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="expertise-rating">Expertise Rating</h4>Expertise was changed to no longer grant reduction to <i>both</i> the target's ability to dodge <i>and</i> parry. When reaching 7.5% Expertise, you will have removed the boss's chance to dodge, but their chance to parry remains unchanged. You'll need an additional 7.5% Expertise to eliminate their chance to parry (15% total). <br/>
<br/>This means that while tanking a target, there is effectively no "soft cap" where Expertise starts dropping off in value. However, as you're not always dealing damage to a target head-on, it's still worth thinking about Expertise in terms of soft cap and hard cap. It's worth noting that if Shield Slam and Revenge is dodged or parried, they grant no Rage.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Gemming for Protection Warrior</span></h2>Your gems will alternate depending on what you and your raid prioritize. We generally have 3 different playstyles (<i>Offensive</i>, <i>Balanced</i>, and <i>Defensive</i>), and below you'll find the appropriate gems for each playstyle. We generally opt to socket for the socket bonus, but if the bonus does not offer an attractive bonus, then opt for the<b> main gem</b> of each category. <br/>
<br/>
<b>
<span class="q5">Legendary Meta Gem:</span></b> In Phase 4 of Mists of Pandaria, we get access to two new meta gems that provide far greater utility than the normal meta gems. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> and <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Capacitive Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Capacitive Primal Diamond</span></a> are the two we can realistically use, and for most people, it should not be much of a choice. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95344/indomitable-primal-diamond">
<img alt="Indomitable Primal Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_legendary_chimeraoffear.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Indomitable Primal Diamond</span></a> provides the most utility overall with an outrageously high uptime, north of 50%. <a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=95346/capacitive-primal-diamond">
